  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member, I want the app to check my saved session against the forum when it starts or resumes, so that an expired login is refreshed or reported instead of failing silently later. LOT-044 (#70, merged as d254b20) shipped the engine flow; the app still uses the placeholder `LocalSessionCheck`.\n\nScope\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Accounts/AccountServices.swift:35-44`: implement `SessionChecking` with LOT-044's `SessionRefreshFlow` / `SessionHealth`, and inject it in `AppEnvironment`. Delete `LocalSessionCheck`, or keep it for previews only.\n- Map the outcomes to the account UI:\n  - valid → nothing;\n  - needs login → the LOT-081 re-login prompt;\n  - unknown page or network error → keep the account logged in, never log out (LOT-044 rule), with a quiet retry.\n\nDepends on: LOT-044 (#70), LOT-081 (#99). MVP: yes, before TestFlight (LOT-161 #251).\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- `@MainActor` model tests with the LOT-044 capture-backed stubs (valid, stale, unknown page, network error); each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- No logout on an unknown page or an error.\n- `xcodebuild build test` green on iPhone and iPad (iOS 27.0) and in CI.\n\nBefore you start: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/lots/LOT-044-*.md, LOT-081 spec, App/README.md.\n",
